</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, MITSUNARI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TDK CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA HIROTADA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAITA YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITOH YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI MITSUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HIROTADA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAITA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITOH, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, MITSUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A driver for driving an organic EL display without causing contrast degradation and erroneous emission, having a simple structure and comprising at least one set of scanning electrodes (COM1, COM2), a data electrode, and an organic layer provided between the electrodes and containing at least an organic material concerning the emission function. A closed circuit is formed through at least one set of electrodes. During the drive of the scanning electrodes (COM1, COM2) and the data electrode, after one electrode is driven and before the next one is driven, there is a predetermined non-selection time (Toff). A driving method is also disclosed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un circuit d'attaque permettant de commander un affichage électroluminescent organique sans provoquer de dégradation de contraste ni d'émission erronée. Ce circuit présente une simple structure et comprend au moins un ensemble d'électrodes de balayage (COM1, COM2), une électrode de données, et une couche organique prévue entre les électrodes et renfermant au moins un matériau organique concernant la fonction d'émission. Un circuit fermé est formé par au moins un ensemble d'électrodes. Pendant la commande des électrodes de balayage (COM1, COM2) et de l'électrode de données, avant la commande d'une électrode et de l'électrode suivante, un temps de non sélection (Toff) est prédéterminé. L'invention concerne également un procédé de commande.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>